{\bf Context.} {\bf This research addresses the growth of holomorphic functions defined on the complex unit ball.}
{\bf {\bf Main results.}} {\bf We prove that $H_q^p$ hypercontractivity holds for the Gaussian measure on the complex unit ball and for weighted versions of the Berman space. Additionally, we demonstrate corresponding isoperimetric inequalities.}
{\bf {\bf New results.}} {\bf We introduce new $H_q^p$ hypercontractive inequalities specifically for the Gaussian measure on the complex unit ball and for weighted Berman spaces.}
{\bf {\bf Novelty.}} {\bf We offer a novel approach to proving hypercontractivity on the complex unit ball by utilizing random walks on the real unit ball.}
{\bf {\bf Significance.}} {\bf Our methodology provides a distinct perspective on the longstanding issue regarding contractive inequalities on the complex unit ball.}
{\bf {\bf Implications.}} {\bf The techniques employed can be applied to other domains, such as the complex polydisc.}
